### Claude on Microsoft Foundry - raw HTTP calls
### Open with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy the equivalent curl
### commands from docs/07-troubleshooting.md.
###
### Fill these in from .deployment-outputs.json (written by scripts/deploy.ps1).

@foundryResource = claudedemo-demo-abc123
@apimName        = claudedemo-demo-abc123
@model           = claude-sonnet-4-6

@directBase  = https://{{foundryResource}}.services.ai.azure.com/anthropic
@gatewayBase = https://{{apimName}}.azure-api.net/anthropic

### Secrets. Prefer the Entra requests below; these exist to show both work.
### az cognitiveservices account keys list -n <account> -g <rg> --query key1 -o tsv
@foundryKey = <foundry-account-key>
### az rest --method post --uri /subscriptions/<sub>/resourceGroups/<rg>/providers/Microsoft.ApiManagement/service/<apim>/subscriptions/claude-code-demo/listSecrets?api-version=2024-05-01 --query primaryKey -o tsv
@gatewayKey = <apim-subscription-key>

### Microsoft Entra ID token for the Anthropic surface of Foundry.
### az account get-access-token --resource https://ai.azure.com --query accessToken -o tsv
@entraToken = <bearer-token>


### 1. DIRECT + API key
POST {{directBase}}/v1/messages
api-key: {{foundryKey}}
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "max_tokens": 200,
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one sentence." }]
}


### 2. DIRECT + Microsoft Entra ID
POST {{directBase}}/v1/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{entraToken}}
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "max_tokens": 200,
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one sentence." }]
}


### 3. GATEWAY + API Management subscription key
### The subscription key header is 'api-key' by default so client code is
### identical to the direct path. See gatewaySubscriptionKeyHeader in the outputs.
POST {{gatewayBase}}/v1/messages
api-key: {{gatewayKey}}
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "max_tokens": 200,
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one sentence." }]
}


### 4. GATEWAY + Microsoft Entra ID
### Requires client-auth-mode = entra or either. The gateway validates the token,
### then either forwards it (passthrough) or swaps it for its managed identity.
POST {{gatewayBase}}/v1/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{entraToken}}
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "max_tokens": 200,
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one sentence." }]
}


### 5. GATEWAY + streaming (proves buffer-response="false" works)
POST {{gatewayBase}}/v1/messages
api-key: {{gatewayKey}}
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "max_tokens": 400,
  "stream": true,
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Count from 1 to 20." }]
}


### 6. Token counting (no inference charge, useful for governance demos)
POST {{gatewayBase}}/v1/messages/count_tokens
api-key: {{gatewayKey}}
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "How many tokens is this?" }]
}


### 7. List models available on the endpoint
GET {{directBase}}/v1/models
Authorization: Bearer {{entraToken}}
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
